 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 518323,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Chione decides to put new siding on her house. She finds that it will cost about $27,800. She decides to begin saving for the purchase so that she doesn’t take on debt to side the house. How much would Chione need to deposit each quarter in an ordinary annuity that yields 5.16% compounded quarterly for 5 years?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$1,227.30"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>To compute the payment to reach a final goal, the payment (<i>pmt</i>) of an ordinary annuity to reach a specific future value (<i>FV</i>) is <span data-math=\"pmt = \\frac{{FV \\times \\frac{r}{n}}}{{{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)}^{n \\times t}} - 1}}\"></span>, where <i>r</i> is the annual interest rate (in decimal form), <i>n</i> is the number of compounding periods per year, and <i>t</i> is the number of years. Round up!</p>\n<p>Once again, it will help you get the right answer using your calculator to find <span data-math=\"n \\times t\"></span> first.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"n \\times t = \\left( 4 \\right)\\left( 5 \\right) = 20\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"pmt = \\frac{{\\left( {27,800 \\times \\frac{{0.0516}}{4}} \\right)}}{{\\left( {{{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.0516}}{4}} \\right)}^{20}} - 1} \\right)}} = \\$1,227.30\"></span></p>\n<p>Additional parentheses were added to help you enter the expression properly in your calculator.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
